{\an8}<i>♪ Now, look, if I step into the world
We can have some fun ♪</i>

20
00:01:12,374 --> 00:01:13,209
<i>♪ Yo ♪</i>

21
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:15,836
<i>♪ Uh, move the world, move, move ♪</i>

22
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,631
<i>♪ Now, look, if I step into the world
Let you have some fun ♪</i>

23
00:01:24,553 --> 00:01:25,554
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah ♪</i>

24
00:01:27,306 --> 00:01:28,224
{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:36,315
- [squishing]
- [Legoshi grunting, panting]

26
00:01:38,442 --> 00:01:40,820
[slurring] From now on... [panting]

27
00:01:41,654 --> 00:01:42,863
I don't need fangs!

28
00:01:42,947 --> 00:01:43,906
[fangs clatter]

29
00:01:45,991 --> 00:01:47,701
Now with those out of the way,

30
00:01:47,785 --> 00:01:50,412
I've earned the right
to give you a good punch!

31
00:01:50,496 --> 00:01:51,664
- [yells]
- [Yahya grunts]

32
00:01:54,416 --> 00:01:56,919
[breathes heavily]

33
00:01:57,962 --> 00:01:59,296
[laughs]

34
00:02:00,172 --> 00:02:02,508
I thought that it'd be worth it
to let it land.

35
00:02:02,591 --> 00:02:05,761
[sighs] But what an utterly
pathetic strike.

36
00:02:05,845 --> 00:02:09,473
If you meant for your punch to be
as weak as your personality, well done.

37
00:02:09,557 --> 00:02:10,975
[grunts, spits]

38
00:02:11,684 --> 00:02:14,562
[Yahya] <i>Your fangs are gone,
but not your strength.</i>

39
00:02:14,645 --> 00:02:18,732
<i>No, on the contrary, I see you rising.</i>

40
00:02:19,316 --> 00:02:22,570
<i>Your spirit can carry you up
through the ranks of the carnivores</i>

41
00:02:22,653 --> 00:02:24,572
<i>until you reign at the top.</i>

42
00:02:25,281 --> 00:02:27,575
[fire alarm ringing]

43
00:02:28,159 --> 00:02:29,326
[chuckles]

44
00:02:29,410 --> 00:02:32,705
It does appear we'll have some guests
from down below.

45
00:02:32,788 --> 00:02:33,622
Huh?

46
00:02:34,832 --> 00:02:37,418
[slurring] We carnivores
are also capable of reason,

47
00:02:38,043 --> 00:02:39,712
and every one of us is suffering.

48
00:02:40,796 --> 00:02:43,382
It just isn't right,
what you're trying to do.

49
00:02:43,465 --> 00:02:46,260
I only punched you
because I was trying to make a point.

50
00:02:47,636 --> 00:02:52,141
But I did disrespect the Beastar.
I am sorry for that.

51
00:02:52,975 --> 00:02:55,102
I got to... I got to go.

52
00:02:55,185 --> 00:02:56,562
[fire alarm ringing]

53
00:02:56,645 --> 00:02:59,440
[receptionist] Mr. Yahya, I heard
the fire alarm. Is everything okay?

54
00:02:59,523 --> 00:03:00,482
[Yahya sighs]

55
00:03:01,483 --> 00:03:03,694
[Yahya] It's all right,
a candle fell over.

56
00:03:03,777 --> 00:03:04,945
[ringing stops]

57
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:12,161
<i>I am finding you
more and more intriguing, Legoshi.</i>

58
00:03:14,204 --> 00:03:19,126
THE GUY BORN IN SPRING

59
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,381
[Gohin, muffled] Try following my finger
with your eyes. Hmm?

60
00:03:25,174 --> 00:03:26,008
Hey.

61
00:03:27,259 --> 00:03:28,260
No good.

62
00:03:28,344 --> 00:03:30,471
- [soft groaning]
- Can you hear me at least?

63
00:03:31,555 --> 00:03:34,642
[groaning continues]

64
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:39,688
[Gohin] Hmm. There don't seem to be
any symptoms of Kines.

65
00:03:39,772 --> 00:03:42,775
[panicked gasping]

66
00:03:45,402 --> 00:03:47,529
- [Gohin] There you are.
- [gasping]

67
00:03:47,613 --> 00:03:50,407
[chuckles] Take it easy, now.
I'm a doctor.

68
00:03:50,491 --> 00:03:53,369
One famous for his radical treatments,
but still.

69
00:03:53,452 --> 00:03:54,912
[chuckles]

70
00:03:54,995 --> 00:03:57,206
Let's you and me try to get along, hmm?

71
00:03:57,706 --> 00:03:59,792
- [soft groaning]
- Huh?

72
00:04:00,918 --> 00:04:02,795
- Oh, you're awake.
- [Legoshi groans]

73
00:04:03,504 --> 00:04:04,588
[muffled] Mr. Gohin?

74
00:04:04,672 --> 00:04:07,967
Don't try to talk.
You're going to need a few days.

75
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:10,094
Huh? Huh?

76
00:04:11,178 --> 00:04:14,181
- [muffled screaming, groaning]
- [laughing]

77
00:04:14,265 --> 00:04:15,933
Oh, and don't touch your face.

78
00:04:17,017 --> 00:04:19,395
- [gasping]
- Whoa now!

79
00:04:19,478 --> 00:04:21,146
- [yelps]
- I'm warning you.

80
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:24,358
I won't go easy on you
just because you're a gal. Okay?

81
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:27,278
It could be worse, so don't be stupid.

82
00:04:27,361 --> 00:04:28,487
- [spits]
- [grunts]

83
00:04:29,488 --> 00:04:30,406
Hmm.

84
00:04:30,948 --> 00:04:32,157
Seriously?

85
00:04:33,659 --> 00:04:35,661
[amusing music playing]

86
00:04:36,662 --> 00:04:39,373
Sorry about this,
but our rooms are all full right now.

87
00:04:39,456 --> 00:04:42,543
- [pen rasping]
- [Gohin exhales]

88
00:04:44,670 --> 00:04:45,754
WHAT DID THAT FOX DO?

89
00:04:45,838 --> 00:04:48,299
Ah, devouring incident. Some rabbit.

90
00:04:48,382 --> 00:04:50,009
[Legoshi] Mmm. Mmm.

91
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:53,554
You know, you gave me quite a shock,

92
00:04:53,637 --> 00:04:56,682
collapsing at my front door
in such bad shape.

93
00:04:56,765 --> 00:04:59,143
[scoffs] Who messed you up so bad?

94
00:04:59,226 --> 00:05:01,312
[Legoshi] Mmm-hmm. Mmm.

95
00:05:04,064 --> 00:05:05,774
{\an8}I PULLED MY FANGS OUT
AND PUNCHED MR. YAHYA

96
00:05:05,858 --> 00:05:07,693
Yahya? What?

97
00:05:07,776 --> 00:05:10,529
What the hell are you doing,
picking a fight like that?

98
00:05:10,612 --> 00:05:12,197
[Legoshi] Hmm.

99
00:05:12,281 --> 00:05:14,158
I'LL WRITE UP A DETAILED REPORT

100
00:05:14,241 --> 00:05:16,410
Spare me, I don't have
the time to read it.

101
00:05:17,036 --> 00:05:20,289
I'm too damn busy dealing with
all these Kines patients anyway.

102
00:05:20,372 --> 00:05:21,373
[Legoshi urging]

103
00:05:22,207 --> 00:05:23,959
{\an8}KINES IS A MEAT NARCOTIC!

104
00:05:24,543 --> 00:05:27,171
Hmm? And you're certain of this?

105
00:05:27,254 --> 00:05:28,172
[Legoshi] Mmm-hmm.

106
00:05:29,089 --> 00:05:30,674
I'LL WRITE UP A DETAILED REPORT

107
00:05:30,758 --> 00:05:32,926
[sighs] Fine.

108
00:05:33,761 --> 00:05:36,847
In any case, rest here
until the swelling goes down, okay?

109
00:05:36,930 --> 00:05:37,848
[Legoshi grunts]

110
00:05:38,766 --> 00:05:39,600
[music ends]

111
00:05:39,683 --> 00:05:40,726
[sighs]

112
00:05:42,186 --> 00:05:43,020
[sighs]

113
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:46,899
GIANT PANDA

114
00:05:52,905 --> 00:05:54,573
[Gohin] Hmm. Mornin'.

115
00:05:59,328 --> 00:06:00,871
[grunts]

116
00:06:00,954 --> 00:06:01,830
[sighs]

117
00:06:03,415 --> 00:06:06,293
So, listen, there are two types
of devourers.

118
00:06:07,669 --> 00:06:10,130
There's the type
that craves more meat afterward

119
00:06:10,214 --> 00:06:13,008
and the type that feels too guilty
to want it again.

120
00:06:13,092 --> 00:06:16,053
The treatment's different
depending on which type you are.

121
00:06:21,266 --> 00:06:23,393
Why don't we talk about last night?

122
00:06:23,477 --> 00:06:26,814
You devoured a living rabbit
in an alley off of Center Street.

123
00:06:27,648 --> 00:06:29,233
Were they someone you knew?

124
00:06:29,316 --> 00:06:31,652
[shuddering]

125
00:06:33,654 --> 00:06:35,697
- Doctor... [shudders]
- Huh?

126
00:06:37,157 --> 00:06:40,119
You know if you want me,
I'll let you take me.

127
00:06:41,537 --> 00:06:43,413
- Hmm.
- Please, doctor.

128
00:06:43,497 --> 00:06:45,791
- Wha--
- Please! Just do it!

129
00:06:45,874 --> 00:06:46,917
Are you really that afraid

130
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,920
- to face up to what you've done? Huh?
- Come on! I'm begging you! [yelps]

131
00:06:50,462 --> 00:06:54,341
[whimpering] Doctor! Just let me go!

132
00:06:54,424 --> 00:06:56,468
Take me and be done with it!

133
00:06:56,552 --> 00:06:58,846
- [Legoshi] Mmm.
- [Ai] I'm begging you! Please!

134
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,265
And screw you!

135
00:07:01,348 --> 00:07:04,184
- Why are you doing this? Why?
- [Gohin] Hey! Listen to me!

136
00:07:04,268 --> 00:07:05,561
Even if I was interested,

137
00:07:05,644 --> 00:07:08,230
a roll in the hay with me
won't solve your problem.

138
00:07:09,106 --> 00:07:11,525
It's important to understand
what made you do it.

139
00:07:11,608 --> 00:07:15,320
If you can't figure that out,
your heart is going to hurt forever.

140
00:07:17,281 --> 00:07:19,074
My heart's always going to hurt...

141
00:07:20,117 --> 00:07:21,243
until I die?

142
00:07:21,952 --> 00:07:23,203
That's right.

143
00:07:24,288 --> 00:07:26,039
So what I want you to do

144
00:07:26,123 --> 00:07:29,501
is take a deep breath and start trying
to come to terms with what you did,

145
00:07:29,585 --> 00:07:31,795
even if the process
of getting there is hard.

146
00:07:32,629 --> 00:07:34,423
[Legoshi sighs]

147
00:07:35,466 --> 00:07:37,593
[Gohin] All right, tell me about yourself.

148
00:07:38,635 --> 00:07:39,928
[Ai] Where do I start?

149
00:07:41,096 --> 00:07:42,723
[Gohin] Wherever. I got all day.

150
00:07:47,352 --> 00:07:48,687
[loudly] Huh?

151
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:51,398
What do you mean Yahya wanted you
to apologize for eating meat?

152
00:07:51,482 --> 00:07:52,483
What's his deal?

153
00:07:53,066 --> 00:07:56,445
Guess he's becoming more and more
of a stickler as he gets older.

154
00:07:57,529 --> 00:07:59,865
You know, he had a partner
when he was younger.

155
00:07:59,948 --> 00:08:03,785
Carrot and stick. Balanced each other out
like they were made for each other.

156
00:08:03,869 --> 00:08:04,870
[Legoshi] Mmm.

157
00:08:05,996 --> 00:08:08,248
[groans] Heard he was a piece of work.

158
00:08:08,332 --> 00:08:10,667
Venomous monitor lizard
by the name of, uh...

159
00:08:10,751 --> 00:08:12,002
[Legoshi] Hmm?

160
00:08:12,085 --> 00:08:14,963
Go... hin. No, that would be me.

161
00:08:15,797 --> 00:08:18,425
Gosha, yeah. That might've been it.

162
00:08:18,509 --> 00:08:20,260
[Legoshi] <i>Huh? My grandpa?</i>

163
00:08:21,553 --> 00:08:22,638
<i>- Hmm.</i>
- What is it?

164
00:08:22,721 --> 00:08:23,722
<i>I get it now.</i>

165
00:08:24,681 --> 00:08:27,100
<i>Huh. That's why he was so strong.</i>

166
00:08:28,185 --> 00:08:30,521
Rumor has it
they had a fight and that was it.

167
00:08:30,604 --> 00:08:31,855
Maybe things would be different

168
00:08:31,939 --> 00:08:33,815
if that old lizard
were still around today.

169
00:08:34,858 --> 00:08:35,817
Hmm.

170
00:08:35,901 --> 00:08:39,446
<i>What happened
between my grandpa and Yahya?</i>

171
00:08:40,364 --> 00:08:41,532
Hmm.

172
00:08:47,579 --> 00:08:50,582
[Corne] I finally figured out
the location of the photo.

173
00:08:50,666 --> 00:08:53,001
It's a multi-tenant building
on Center Street.

174
00:08:53,085 --> 00:08:54,711
[Yahya] And was the ivory there?

175
00:08:55,212 --> 00:08:58,507
[Corne] No. But I did notice
something strange.

176
00:08:59,675 --> 00:09:03,387
When you overlay the floor plans
of each and every floor in this building...

177
00:09:04,137 --> 00:09:06,723
Let's see... Oh, yeah, there it is.

178
00:09:07,224 --> 00:09:08,308
This part.

179
00:09:08,392 --> 00:09:10,477
No doors, no windows, just a space,

180
00:09:10,561 --> 00:09:12,980
and it runs all the way down
to the basement.

181
00:09:13,063 --> 00:09:14,189
Hmm.

182
00:09:15,524 --> 00:09:18,569
That herbivore counselor's office
on the fifth floor...

183
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:21,863
[Corne] That is one big-ass sofa.

184
00:09:23,323 --> 00:09:24,992
[Yahya] Zoom in on the fireplace.

185
00:09:26,201 --> 00:09:27,244
Right on the floor.

186
00:09:29,371 --> 00:09:32,040
Hmm. Now back to the fireplace.

187
00:09:34,126 --> 00:09:35,085
Hold on.

188
00:09:36,128 --> 00:09:37,337
Who's that on the right?

189
00:09:38,797 --> 00:09:40,090
Oh, that's the counselor.

190
00:09:40,674 --> 00:09:42,092
[Yahya] A gazelle, huh?

191
00:09:44,094 --> 00:09:47,681
So the elephant lowers its guard
around a fellow herbivore.

192
00:09:47,764 --> 00:09:51,810
They kill the elephant, drop the body
down the hole in the fireplace,

193
00:09:51,893 --> 00:09:53,478
then cut it up in the basement.

194
00:09:54,479 --> 00:09:57,190
That's when they remove the ivory
and prep it for sale.

195
00:09:57,691 --> 00:09:59,401
That's their modus operandi.

196
00:09:59,484 --> 00:10:02,946
But right in the middle
of a huge shopping district?

197
00:10:03,614 --> 00:10:04,656
[Yahya sighs]

198
00:10:06,325 --> 00:10:09,411
<i>Is someone deliberately
trying to challenge me?</i>

199
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:19,171
- [Gohin] Wow, you really are a big help!
- [Legoshi chuckles]

200
00:10:19,254 --> 00:10:21,089
[slurring] Well, I am a stagehand.

201
00:10:21,173 --> 00:10:23,842
Nah, it's more than touching up the paint.

202
00:10:23,925 --> 00:10:27,638
- There was also the Kines report.
- [chuckles] You're really too nice.

203
00:10:27,721 --> 00:10:31,016
I should honestly be apologizing.
I stayed for a whole week.

204
00:10:31,099 --> 00:10:34,645
- [chuckles] Ah, Legoshi. Here.
- Hmm? Huh.

205
00:10:35,562 --> 00:10:36,480
Huh?

206
00:10:36,563 --> 00:10:39,733
[Gohin] These should help you
speak properly, and eat too.

207
00:10:39,816 --> 00:10:41,234
Ah!

208
00:10:41,318 --> 00:10:44,404
- Uh, thanks, but I don't need those.
- Huh?

209
00:10:44,488 --> 00:10:46,323
I was serious
when I pulled out my own fangs.

210
00:10:46,406 --> 00:10:49,159
It's not a decision
I intend to turn back from.

211
00:10:49,242 --> 00:10:50,994
I don't need those replacements.

212
00:10:51,078 --> 00:10:52,788
How are you going to eat?

213
00:10:52,871 --> 00:10:54,790
I can live off rice porridge.

214
00:10:54,873 --> 00:10:56,583
And how will you find yourself a girl?

215
00:10:56,667 --> 00:10:58,502
I'll be a virgin all my life anyway.

216
00:10:58,585 --> 00:11:01,838
[growling in frustration]

217
00:11:02,673 --> 00:11:03,715
[sighs wearily]

218
00:11:04,549 --> 00:11:07,552
Legoshi, I'm not saying
you have to wear 'em,

219
00:11:07,636 --> 00:11:09,054
but at least try 'em on.

220
00:11:10,931 --> 00:11:12,516
- [groaning]
- Legoshi!

221
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:16,269
If you're really going to be
that insistent, then I'll give 'em a try.

222
00:11:17,312 --> 00:11:20,023
- [clicking]
- [Legoshi groaning softly]

223
00:11:22,526 --> 00:11:23,777
[slurps, gulps]

224
00:11:26,113 --> 00:11:28,824
[Gohin chuckles] Well?

225
00:11:28,907 --> 00:11:32,119
[in normal voice] Huh. Honestly,
they feel just right. [chuckles]

226
00:11:33,286 --> 00:11:34,413
[sighs]

227
00:11:35,288 --> 00:11:37,457
I wanted to be strong
without having to use my fangs.

228
00:11:37,541 --> 00:11:39,960
That's the whole reason
I was training under you.

229
00:11:40,043 --> 00:11:43,171
[inhales, exhales]
And the way things shook out,

230
00:11:43,255 --> 00:11:45,966
you managed to win
a life-or-death fight against a bear

231
00:11:46,049 --> 00:11:47,759
only by eating your friend's leg.

232
00:11:48,510 --> 00:11:49,845
If you've come this far already,

233
00:11:49,928 --> 00:11:52,472
why not accept yourself
as the wolf you are?

234
00:11:52,556 --> 00:11:56,768
Okay, so, after seeing
Yahya's overwhelming presence,

235
00:11:56,852 --> 00:12:00,313
the first place I thought to run to
was the Black Market.

236
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:05,026
<i>If I have subconsciously let this place
become my safe space, then...</i>

237
00:12:05,902 --> 00:12:07,612
<i>doesn't that make me a hypocrite?</i>

238
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:12,075
If that's really how you feel right now,

239
00:12:12,159 --> 00:12:14,870
I encourage you to spend some time
thinking it through.

240
00:12:15,537 --> 00:12:16,663
Right. [sighs softly]

241
00:12:17,247 --> 00:12:18,415
Thank you very much.

242
00:12:19,332 --> 00:12:20,584
[Gohin exhales]

243
00:12:24,379 --> 00:12:26,381
[mellow piano music playing]

244
00:12:28,341 --> 00:12:29,509
Tibetan sand foxes

245
00:12:29,593 --> 00:12:32,971
have a reputation for not showing
their emotions on their face.

246
00:12:33,054 --> 00:12:35,015
Made it hard to tell if you were ready.

247
00:12:36,141 --> 00:12:40,228
I was a challenge, but even then,
you chose to fight through and help me.

248
00:12:40,979 --> 00:12:44,065
It was only as I regained my emotions
that I realized that.

249
00:12:44,983 --> 00:12:47,068
You've been working hard, Ai.

250
00:12:49,279 --> 00:12:51,615
But the more time
I spent with you, doctor,

251
00:12:51,698 --> 00:12:54,075
the more I could feel my guilt
weighing me down.

252
00:12:54,159 --> 00:12:58,246
It sounds to me like you're not at risk
of devouring someone ever again.

253
00:12:59,414 --> 00:13:01,291
- [Ai] Doctor?
- Hmm?

254
00:13:02,751 --> 00:13:03,627
I'm going...

255
00:13:05,378 --> 00:13:07,422
to turn myself in to the police.

256
00:13:09,174 --> 00:13:11,718
[Gohin breathes heavily]

257
00:13:14,262 --> 00:13:16,264
[sobbing]

258
00:13:18,141 --> 00:13:18,975
Hey now.

259
00:13:20,519 --> 00:13:23,146
That's emotion,
but I wish it were a smile.

260
00:13:23,939 --> 00:13:25,899
You're the one who should be smiling.

261
00:13:25,982 --> 00:13:29,319
You said the best route is for the patient
to turn themselves in, right?

262
00:13:29,402 --> 00:13:31,947
Well, may be best for society.

263
00:13:33,073 --> 00:13:36,910
Still, for now,
you'll just have to let me be sad.

264
00:13:37,786 --> 00:13:41,206
Then I'm going to leave my smile
with you for a while.

265
00:13:41,289 --> 00:13:42,123
Hmm?

266
00:13:42,207 --> 00:13:46,086
I'll leave you with a smile, and you can
give it back to me when I get out.

267
00:13:46,169 --> 00:13:49,256
Well? What do you say
we call it a promise?

268
00:13:49,339 --> 00:13:51,049
[laughs]

269
00:13:51,132 --> 00:13:54,219
It would have to be a fantastic smile
for me to agree to that.

270
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:55,971
[Ai chuckles softly]

271
00:13:56,846 --> 00:13:58,306
[Gohin] Come back soon, okay?

272
00:14:00,559 --> 00:14:04,938
PLANT PRODUCTION RESEARCH FACILITY

273
00:14:05,021 --> 00:14:06,439
[Haru] Wow. [chuckles]

274
00:14:07,148 --> 00:14:09,734
This university
really does have everything.

275
00:14:09,818 --> 00:14:12,904
[Lisa] You mean for the plants?
You sure love them, don't you, Haru?

276
00:14:12,988 --> 00:14:15,448
- Huh? Do you not?
- It's not that.

277
00:14:15,532 --> 00:14:18,577
I only enrolled here because I heard
it helps when looking for a job.

278
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,578
What about you?

279
00:14:19,661 --> 00:14:21,997
Well, I want to open a restaurant.

280
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,748
- Seriously?
- That's right.

281
00:14:23,832 --> 00:14:27,168
I want to serve vegetables
that carnivores will find delicious too.

282
00:14:27,711 --> 00:14:29,129
- What?
- Well, think about it.

283
00:14:29,212 --> 00:14:32,465
If everyone could share the same meals,
wouldn't that be fun?

284
00:14:32,549 --> 00:14:35,594
Honestly, that's sort of what
I'm hoping to study here.

285
00:14:35,677 --> 00:14:38,179
You really are something else, Haru.
You know that?

286
00:14:43,852 --> 00:14:45,520
Hello there, new students.

287
00:14:45,604 --> 00:14:49,316
Allow me to welcome you to today's lesson
on edible plants and taste.

288
00:14:49,399 --> 00:14:50,525
- [chuckles]
- [pigeon] Yeah.

289
00:14:51,902 --> 00:14:55,864
I... I see that you're all herbivores.
Very good. [chuckles]

290
00:14:55,947 --> 00:14:58,325
We won't have
any of those nasty brutes in here,

291
00:14:58,408 --> 00:15:00,035
stinking up our beautiful plants.

292
00:15:00,118 --> 00:15:00,952
Thank God.

293
00:15:01,036 --> 00:15:02,746
- [students chuckle]
- Huh? Hmph.

294
00:15:03,622 --> 00:15:05,332
And as our first topic,

295
00:15:05,415 --> 00:15:09,252
we herbivores possess far more
refined palates than carnivores do.

296
00:15:09,336 --> 00:15:13,214
There are flavors we enjoy that carnivores
are unable to even begin to detect.

297
00:15:13,298 --> 00:15:15,133
Their palates are as barbaric as they are.

298
00:15:15,842 --> 00:15:17,427
[exclaims in disappointment]

299
00:15:17,510 --> 00:15:19,346
- You're being discriminatory.
- Huh?

300
00:15:19,429 --> 00:15:20,305
[all gasp]

301
00:15:20,388 --> 00:15:24,184
My boyfriend tells me how hurt he is
by that sort of casual hate speech.

302
00:15:24,267 --> 00:15:26,853
It's inappropriate
in a so-called place of higher learning.

303
00:15:26,937 --> 00:15:28,688
Uh, that's true.

304
00:15:28,772 --> 00:15:31,399
How right you are. [nervously]
Do forgive me.

305
00:15:32,025 --> 00:15:33,485
You're dating a carnivore?

306
00:15:33,568 --> 00:15:35,528
You should really try it for yourself.

307
00:15:35,612 --> 00:15:37,864
You'd be amazed at how it opens your eyes.

308
00:15:37,948 --> 00:15:40,367
[pigeon] Let's try to start this lesson
on the right foot.

309
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:41,326
[Ako] Hmm.

310
00:15:44,496 --> 00:15:46,331
[Lisa] Ako, you're just amazing.

311
00:15:46,414 --> 00:15:50,168
- You were so cool back there.
- Well? What happened? I want to hear.

312
00:15:50,251 --> 00:15:54,506
Not a lot. I just told the professor that
his way of thinking is so last century.

313
00:15:54,589 --> 00:15:58,093
People see love between carnivores
and herbivores as dangerous,

314
00:15:58,176 --> 00:16:01,930
but if a couple understands each other
as well as we do, it can totally work out.

315
00:16:02,013 --> 00:16:05,183
- [Haru] You shouldn't say that so lightly.
- [scoffs] Huh?

316
00:16:06,309 --> 00:16:07,936
If it truly were that easy,

317
00:16:08,019 --> 00:16:10,772
if simply understanding
was all a relationship needed,

318
00:16:10,855 --> 00:16:14,609
then our society wouldn't have to
deal with so many devouring incidents.

319
00:16:14,693 --> 00:16:17,404
I don't know if you just haven't
realized it yet, but...

320
00:16:17,988 --> 00:16:20,115
the heart can't overcome instinct.

321
00:16:20,824 --> 00:16:22,325
Can you truly love him fully

322
00:16:22,409 --> 00:16:24,911
even when his body
continues to crave meat?

323
00:16:26,788 --> 00:16:28,665
I've been wondering about you.

324
00:16:28,748 --> 00:16:31,167
The only reason you're dating
in the first place

325
00:16:31,251 --> 00:16:33,169
is to make a fashion statement, right?

326
00:16:33,253 --> 00:16:34,796
[Ako] Excuse me?

327
00:16:35,714 --> 00:16:37,549
[quirky music playing]

328
00:16:37,632 --> 00:16:38,925
[Eado] Hey, wait up!

329
00:16:39,009 --> 00:16:41,261
I get you're mad,
but don't take it out on me.

330
00:16:41,344 --> 00:16:43,221
I don't get why you're not mad too.

331
00:16:43,304 --> 00:16:45,724
You could have given her a growl
or scared her or something.

332
00:16:45,807 --> 00:16:47,559
Instead, you let her embarrass us.

333
00:16:47,642 --> 00:16:48,935
Look, I don't really...

334
00:16:49,686 --> 00:16:52,439
Hey, are you angry
because she saw through us like that?

335
00:16:52,522 --> 00:16:55,358
- That we're dating to make a statement?
- What?

336
00:16:55,442 --> 00:16:57,861
I mean, we're both
kind of messing around here.

337
00:16:57,944 --> 00:17:00,405
There's no need to be
so upset about it, is there?

338
00:17:00,989 --> 00:17:02,532
- Eado.
- Huh?

339
00:17:03,450 --> 00:17:06,661
In the end, you're just another
ordinary lion, aren't you?

340
00:17:06,745 --> 00:17:10,582
Just because you can't see me,
a rabbit, as a female, you can't commit.

341
00:17:10,665 --> 00:17:13,918
If you really think I'm wrong,
then prove it. Give me a kiss!

342
00:17:14,502 --> 00:17:16,004
[chuckles nervously]

343
00:17:16,588 --> 00:17:18,840
[sighs] Well, if you insist.

344
00:17:25,096 --> 00:17:26,097
[Ako moans softly]

345
00:17:27,932 --> 00:17:29,184
[gasps]

346
00:17:30,226 --> 00:17:32,937
Uh-- What do you know, you can commit.

347
00:17:33,021 --> 00:17:35,982
No ordinary lion would dare
turn down a challenge like that.

348
00:17:42,113 --> 00:17:44,115
[mysterious music playing]

349
00:17:59,339 --> 00:18:01,549
[Melon, muffled] <i>Not to worry,
our facilities were built</i>

350
00:18:01,633 --> 00:18:05,345
<i>to accommodate all species,
including elephant patients like yourself.</i>

351
00:18:05,428 --> 00:18:09,432
[elephant] <i>I can't tell you how grateful
I am to talk to an herbivore therapist.</i>

352
00:18:09,516 --> 00:18:10,517
[Melon] <i>No, no.</i>

353
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:13,603
[elephant] <i>I know that some may
find myself as intimidating,</i>

354
00:18:13,686 --> 00:18:17,065
<i>but at the end of the day,
I'm still an herbivore like you.</i>

355
00:18:17,148 --> 00:18:20,443
<i>- Uh, so, um, I hope...</i>
- [Yahya grunts]

356
00:18:20,527 --> 00:18:22,237
[Melon] <i>Oh, no, it's all right.</i>

357
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:24,781
<i>Just take your time
and tell me everything when you're ready.</i>

358
00:18:24,864 --> 00:18:26,991
[elephant crying]

359
00:18:27,951 --> 00:18:29,911
- [Yahya] Hmm.
- [Melon] <i>There, there.</i>

360
00:18:29,994 --> 00:18:32,205
- [Yahya grunts]
- [elephant crying]

361
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,625
- [elephant] <i>I'm so sorry.</i>
- Huh?

362
00:18:35,708 --> 00:18:37,168
<i>- I'm crying.</i>
- [Melon] <i>It's all right.</i>

363
00:18:37,252 --> 00:18:39,254
[elephant] <i>I just think that I...</i> [sobs]

364
00:18:39,337 --> 00:18:40,505
[groans]

365
00:18:40,588 --> 00:18:42,841
- [Melon] Do you have an appointment?
- [groans]

366
00:18:42,924 --> 00:18:46,136
That's so odd,
I must have missed it in my calendar.

367
00:18:47,178 --> 00:18:50,640
But, you know,
I think I can squeeze you right in.

368
00:18:50,723 --> 00:18:54,060
But I'm afraid personal items
must be left at the front desk.

369
00:18:54,144 --> 00:18:56,354
I know exactly what you really are.

370
00:18:56,437 --> 00:18:59,065
[Melon, sarcastically] Wow!
A Beastar knows who I am!

371
00:18:59,149 --> 00:19:01,651
[laughs sarcastically] What an honor.

372
00:19:01,734 --> 00:19:02,861
- [grunts]
- [mask snaps]

373
00:19:02,944 --> 00:19:04,612
[gasps]

374
00:19:04,696 --> 00:19:05,947
Wait, are you--

375
00:19:06,030 --> 00:19:08,116
Oh, I guess you don't know me.

376
00:19:09,325 --> 00:19:10,410
The name's Melon.

377
00:19:11,161 --> 00:19:12,579
- [grunts]
- Remember it.

378
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:16,207
[groans, sighs]

379
00:19:16,791 --> 00:19:18,001
[groans]

380
00:19:18,084 --> 00:19:21,588
Ah, we finally get to meet.
[inhales sharply]

381
00:19:21,671 --> 00:19:23,756
- But now I can't invite you to the party.
- [groaning]

382
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,592
- Shame.
- [grunts]

383
00:19:25,675 --> 00:19:27,635
[yelps] Get back!

384
00:19:27,719 --> 00:19:29,554
[grunts, yelps]

385
00:19:32,390 --> 00:19:33,683
- [thuds]
- [groans loudly]

386
00:19:35,935 --> 00:19:36,936
[music ends]

387
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:39,731
- [indistinct chatter]
- [Haru] <i>Oh, me and my big mouth.</i>

388
00:19:40,481 --> 00:19:43,443
<i>To be fair, I don't think
I said anything that wasn't true.</i>

389
00:19:43,985 --> 00:19:46,404
<i>But calling my friend's relationship out
in public like that?</i>

390
00:19:46,487 --> 00:19:48,198
<i>Oh, I'm the worst.</i>

391
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:51,618
<i>I, uh, was probably just jealous.</i>

392
00:19:51,701 --> 00:19:54,662
<i>They seem to be having fun
as a mixed-species couple.</i>

393
00:19:54,746 --> 00:19:57,332
- [sighs] <i>I should tell Ako I'm sorry.</i>
- [siren wails]

394
00:19:57,415 --> 00:19:58,875
- [goat] What's going on?
- [Haru] Huh?

395
00:19:58,958 --> 00:20:01,169
- [tiger] Sounds like it's bad.
- [siren wails]

396
00:20:01,252 --> 00:20:02,712
[indistinct chatter]

397
00:20:02,795 --> 00:20:04,714
- [Eado] Ako!
- [officer] Get back!

398
00:20:04,797 --> 00:20:06,341
[Eado sobbing]

399
00:20:06,424 --> 00:20:08,593
- [gasps]
- [Eado] I don't know what happened.

400
00:20:09,260 --> 00:20:12,388
- [Eado sobbing]
- [Ako breathing feebly]

401
00:20:13,097 --> 00:20:15,308
I don't... I just...

402
00:20:15,934 --> 00:20:18,311
- [breathing feebly]
- [Haru gasps softly]

403
00:20:18,895 --> 00:20:21,481
I just kissed her
'cause she told me to. [breathes heavily]

404
00:20:21,564 --> 00:20:23,566
I swear I didn't want to eat her!

405
00:20:23,650 --> 00:20:27,111
But I... I just got confused! [sobbing]

406
00:20:29,781 --> 00:20:32,325
- Hey.
- Please! You got to save her! Please!

407
00:20:32,408 --> 00:20:34,160
- [officer 1] Get in there!
- Ako!

408
00:20:34,786 --> 00:20:35,828
[officer 1] Shut up!

409
00:20:35,912 --> 00:20:37,372
- [officer 2] Calm down.
- Ako!

410
00:20:38,206 --> 00:20:41,084
- [car door closes]
- [Haru] <i>The ground is covered in blood.</i>

411
00:20:42,418 --> 00:20:44,921
<i>But today is such a beautiful, sunny day.</i>

412
00:20:49,676 --> 00:20:51,928
[dog] Oh. Watch yourself young lady.

413
00:20:52,762 --> 00:20:55,348
Sorry, it'll leave a stain
if we don't clean it now.

414
00:20:57,934 --> 00:20:59,519
[Haru] <i>Can you love him fully</i>

415
00:20:59,602 --> 00:21:02,105
<i>even when his body
continues to crave meat?</i>

416
00:21:05,733 --> 00:21:07,443
<i>I knew it from the start.</i>

417
00:21:10,154 --> 00:21:12,115
<i>To truly love a carnivore</i>

418
00:21:13,157 --> 00:21:16,202
<i>is to enter a world of pain and suffering.</i>

419
00:21:17,203 --> 00:21:20,832
<i>It's not something simple,
made up of low stakes and little jokes.</i>

420
00:21:21,958 --> 00:21:24,335
<i>But that's why...</i>

421
00:21:25,545 --> 00:21:27,422
<i>That's exactly why I...</i>

422
00:21:29,132 --> 00:21:29,966
[gasps]

423
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,468
[yells]

424
00:21:32,552 --> 00:21:34,470
[yells]

425
00:21:36,639 --> 00:21:39,559
UDON BEBEBE

426
00:21:39,642 --> 00:21:40,852
[newscaster] <i>At around 3:00...</i>

427
00:21:40,935 --> 00:21:42,145
Sorry about the wait.

428
00:21:42,228 --> 00:21:45,690
<i>...an attempted devouring took place
on the campus of Algama University.</i>

429
00:21:45,773 --> 00:21:47,692
<i>- The student was...</i>
- [Legoshi] <i>Haru's school.</i>

430
00:21:47,775 --> 00:21:49,527
<i>...taken from the scene
in critical condition.</i>

431
00:21:49,610 --> 00:21:52,071
<i>But it does seem as though
they're going to pull through.</i>

432
00:21:52,155 --> 00:21:52,989
Huh?

433
00:21:53,072 --> 00:21:55,616
Hey, Legoshi. Happy birthday.

434
00:21:56,117 --> 00:21:59,746
Uh, I just wanted to say that,
so I came by.

435
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

436
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,751
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

437
00:22:04,834 --> 00:22:08,338
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

438
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,425
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

439
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,803
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

440
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

441
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,603
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

442
00:22:23,686 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

443
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,527
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

444
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

445
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,119
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

446
00:22:40,203 --> 00:22:44,832
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

447
00:22:44,916 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

448
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,044
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

449
00:22:48,127 --> 00:22:52,548
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

450
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

451
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,765
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

452
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:02,767
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

453
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,185
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

454
00:23:04,894 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

455
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

456
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,693
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

457
00:23:13,444 --> 00:23:16,322
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

458
00:23:17,365 --> 00:23:19,325
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

459
00:23:19,408 --> 00:23:24,330
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>
